{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Two hundred sol[C]diers march to [D]Caesarea
Lysias writes the letter with [G]care [D/F#]
[Em]Brought safely to Felix the [C]governor
[D]He asks what province Paul en[G]dures
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Faith in Christ [C]Jesus he speaks
[D]Righteousness and self con[G]trol
Judgment [G/B]to [C]come makes Felix af[D]raid
That is e[C]nough for [D]now he [G]says
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Five days later Ananias [C]comes
[D]Tertullus lays the charges [G]down [D/F#]
[Em]Paul defends himself with [C]cheer
[D]I worship God according to the [G]Way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Faith in [G/B]Christ [C]Jesus he speaks
[D]Righteousness and self con[G]trol
Judgment [G/B]to [C]come makes Felix af[D]raid
